Z||000000||bHooper||11-12-1999||09:55 PM||||Today was a odd day, I saw 3 fieros... on the <BR>road.  The first was a '84/85 coupe in excellent shape (from my mirror) with a female driver, the second was a SE? with a luggage rack (it did have the SE/Gt fascia) and the third was a worn out coupe.  Not bad, 2 decent cars in a week is a lot in Greensboro!||||reg||10
Z||000001||fiero56||11-12-1999||10:38 PM||||I see Fieros around here onece in a while, not a daily thing, but usually I see one a week.  This week I saw, a grey 84-86 coupe on McEwen, the guy who drives his 86-87 GT down my street everyday around 4:30, and I saw a beautifull red '88? GT(just caught a glimpse) the other day at Paragon and 725. The only one who saw me driving was the guy in the 84-86 coupe. I don't think any of these people are on the Forum as not many people from the Dayton area are on, I know of one.||||reg||7
Z||000002||hefty||11-12-1999||11:03 PM||||I see a couple a week in Columbus, most honk and wave. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fiero56||11-13-1999||06:32 PM||||Funny,<BR>When ever I'm in Columbus and pass a Fiero, I never get a response.  They were all driven by guys, and they wouldn't even give me so mauch as a glance.  Weekly I'd see a white 84-86 coupe and also a grey of the same years, always going the opposite direction.  One day I did see a BEAUTIFULL yellow'88 GT all tricked out.  Had the IRM scoops on it, lots of extras but not TOO much, the guy driving it didn't see me though, he was wactching traffic.  I saw all these cars on Alum Creek on my daily commute to college and back. Usually around the Obetz area.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 11-13-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||four50four||11-13-1999||06:36 PM||||i seen a used to be nice SE on the news today after it was in an accident. Fieros are somewhat of a rarity around here||||reg||7
Z||000005||hefty||11-13-1999||07:42 PM||||Grandview, Arlington area is where I'm at. There are a few that live or work in the area that I see on a regular basis. I used to go four wheelin' around Obetz. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Richard Parnell||11-13-1999||11:17 PM||||I see a 3-4 a week here on oahu. Some wave. Some don't have a clue.  I like seeing them though cause i always think mine's the coolest.||||reg||1
Z||000007||BENGAL4||11-13-1999||11:24 PM||||Hey fiero56,<BR>I got arrested in Obetz once. We had been on High Street at Papa Joe's and on the way home, we relieved ourselves in the graveyard. The police kind of frowned on this.<P>BTW this was in 1982. Some Forum members know that I no longer drink ( Born again Christian now) so I don't want to shock them or make them think I backslid to my old ways. My only 2 vices now are Fiero's and the Bengals.<p>[This message has been edited by BENGAL4 (edited 11-13-1999).]||||reg||10
Z||000008||fiero56||11-13-1999||11:58 PM||||I never had a run in with the police, but the student housing DeVRY used was right at the end of Alum Creek, next to Rikenbacher(sp?) airport.  The FBI stopped at a friends place one night(just a few buildings down), looking for a guy named "Larry". We never did figure that one out. Cops were around there all the time(busting drugees), glad to be out of there. That was the one of the times I was glad to have an alarm on my Fiero(the nicest car in the lot), it was never hit, but had others beside it hit several times, different cars each time.||||reg||7
Z||000009||Gokart||11-14-1999||06:56 AM||||Saw a different Fiero yesterday than the ones that I have seen in my area for the first time in about a month. It was a 2M4 and had same dark red color as my GT. Looked like it needed alot of TLC so I turned around and went back to where it was parked and I dropped one of Cliff's Forum cards in his slightly opened drivers side window!||||reg||6
