Z||000020||Patrick||11-15-1999||11:20 PM||||<BR><B>olympic</B>, I've just got to quiz you a bit on your comment about Fieros being rare in Canada. Are you basing this opinion on what you've observed in Melville, Saskatchewan? This is a <B>HUGE</B> country. I can't speak for anyone living in Calgary or Toronto or Montreal, but here in Vancouver, Fieros are everywhere! I can see half a dozen different ones every day, without even leaving the house! Now granted, I live on a busy street, but it isn't a major thoroughfare.<P>What I haven't seen (or heard) so far is a V8 powered Fiero. Now that would be nice! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000021||Scott2M4||11-16-1999||08:18 AM||||Hey Fiero56 ... I was out looking for you last weekend.  I was driving down 725 (and Centerville Station), Clyo, Spring Valley Pike, Paragon, McEwen, Yankee and Lyons.<P>Didn't recall seeing any Fieros but did get a few looks.  Kinda funny ... before buying mine, I hardly saw any (one of the many reasons I bought it).  Now, I _usually_ see several a week.<P>Speaking of 'The Fiero Card' that Cliff developed ... is it available for purchase or are we to print it from the thread to which it was posted?||||reg||6
